PWA Kit Best Practices Guide

Overview

This document outlines best practices for developing Salesforce Commerce Composable Storefront applications using PWA Kit's core technology stack. It covers React, React Query (TanStack Query), React Testing Library, and general frontend development patterns.

Note: code examples in this docs are not from actual source code.

PWA Kit V3 template-retail-react- app guideline at packages/template-retail-react-app

Technology Stack Summary

Core Dependencies

* React: ^18.2.0 - Modern UI library with concurrent features
* @tanstack/react-query: ^4.28.0 - Data fetching and caching
* @testing-library/react: ^14.0.0 - Component testing utilities
* @chakra-ui/react: ^2.6.0 - UI component library
* @salesforce/commerce-sdk-react: Commerce API integration hooks
* React Router Dom: ^5.3.4 - Client-side routing
* React Hook Form: ^7.43.9 - Form state management

Development

 Workflow

1. Analyze Requirements - Understand the feature requirements
2. Review Existing Code - Look for similar implementations
3. Plan Implementation - Design component structure
4. Implement Incrementally - Build in small steps
5. Test Thoroughly - Write comprehensive tests
6. Review Code Quality - Ensure accessibility and performance


Avoid:

* Re-create a new component before checking current exising UI library (Chakra v2 UI)
* Should NOT putting around a workaround for API the pwa-kit. This needs to be communicated and worked with API teams to get the API working for pwa-kit

