2. Logging

Use pwa-kit logger to create a more context to logs messages. It is a simple wrapper around the native Node.js console. logger has all the methods of native Node.js log. console.log, console.warn, console.info, and the like

 E.g

import logger from '../app/utils/logger-instance'

logger.warn(
    '[DataCloudApi] 400 Bad Request: Check your Data Cloud configuration (appSourceId, tenantId) and event payload.',
    {
        namespace: 'use-datacloud._handleApiError',
        additionalProperties: {error: err?.response}
    }
)


